 "intro": {
  "title": "SOUNDING DEEP HEART",
  "lines": [
   "The bottom of the Deep: a floor like skin, and over it the thing that the Song is kept in.",
   "One conductor stands between you and the stair."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The conductor stopped in the middle of a bar. The forks rang on without it, one at a time, and then they stopped too. Beyond the corridor the stair goes down again, and it is cold.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [7, 44],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The floor is warm. Not heated: warm, like a hand. The wall has a grain, the way a muscle does, and it is moving very slowly in and out."
  },
  {
   "id": "hall",
   "at": [20, 44],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A hall of spears in ranks again, facing the way I came in. They have stopped expecting anyone from the other side."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [32, 44],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: the count of this district, kept on one note. The note is in four forks. It has not been struck since the conductor lost it."
  },
  {
   "id": "heart",
   "at": [47, 44],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "It hangs from the roof on cords as thick as a mast, and it is the size of a house. It is beating, once in about as long as it takes to say so."
  },
  {
   "id": "boss",
   "at": [60, 44],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "One Vael on a round dais with a rod in one hand and the other up in front of its face. It is looking at the forks."
  },
  {
   "id": "ring",
   "at": [56, 44],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Its breath is a ring across the floor, to the wall and back. A pillar stops it going out and coming in. Stand behind one, and keep standing there until the second one has passed."
  },
  {
   "id": "shield",
   "at": [58, 44],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "It takes a twentieth of what you hit it with while any fork stands. The forks are at the corners of the lobe and they can be broken."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [26, 29],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The guard hall wall rings hollow in the north, in a seam of paler skin."
  },
  {
   "id": "seam",
   "at": [26, 25],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "For whoever is sent to stop it. It never wanted to be a conductor, and nobody asked. Do not make it suffer: it has been afraid for a long time."
  },
  {
   "id": "dead",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "It said nothing the whole time. Its last note went out across the floor and, for once, did not come back."
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "at": [90, 44],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A corridor, straight, the first straight thing in the whole Deep. Cold air at the far end. What is below this is not warm."
  },
  {
   "id": "last-call",
   "at": [92, 44],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "Calder, this is the last I can hold. The lamp is lit and the tea is cold. I am here until the set goes."
  }
 ],
